{{also|engravé}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|ingrave}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|eɪv}}

===Etymology 1===
From earlier {{term|ingrave}}, equivalent to {{prefix|en|grave|gloss2=to carve, engrave|lang=-}}. More at {{l|en|grave}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|engrav|ing}}

# {{transitive}} To [[carve]] text or symbols into (something), usually for the purposes of identification or art.
#: ''He '''engraved''' the plaque with his name.''
# {{transitive}} To carve (something) into a material.
#: ''He '''engraved''' his name.''

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|carve (text or symbols) into}} [[carve]], [[etch]], [[inscribe]]

